where Σ ∗ {\displaystyle \Sigma ^{*}} is the Kleene star on Σ {\displaystyle \Sigma }, w L 2 {\displaystyle wL_{2}} is the language formed by concatenating w {\displaystyle w} with each element of L 2 {\displaystyle L_{2}}, and ∅ {\displaystyle \varnothing } is the empty set.

